stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 795.89 Td (A. InvestmentService creates new investments as PENDING and updateStatus converts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 781.89 Td (provided status to uppercase before saving.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 760.89 Td (Q. Why does InvestmentService catch RuntimeException in notifyFounder?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 746.89 Td (A. Investment creation should still succeed even if startup lookup, user lookup,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 732.89 Td (RabbitMQ, or email infrastructure is temporarily unavailable.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 46.00 704.89 Td (Security Questions) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 675.89 Td (Q. How is JWT used in this project?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 661.89 Td (A. Auth service generates JWTs after login. Other services use JWT filters to validate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 647.89 Td (the Authorization header and set the authenticated user in the security context.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 626.89 Td (Q. Why is user id stored as JWT subject?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 612.89 Td (A. Services can identify the logged-in user without calling auth-service for every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 598.89 Td (request.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 577.89 Td (Q. How does TeamService prevent accepting someone elses invitation?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 563.89 Td (A. It compares the authenticated user id with request.userId and allows mismatch only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 549.89 Td (for ROLE_ADMIN.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 528.89 Td (Q. How does MessagingService protect conversations?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 514.89 Td (A. It requires the authenticated user to be a participant when creating a conversation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 500.89 Td (and allows users to view only their own conversation list.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 479.89 Td (Q. What is the risk if services trusted userId from frontend?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 465.89 Td (A. A malicious client could create startups, investments, messages, or team actions on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 451.89 Td (behalf of another user.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 46.00 423.89 Td (Database and JPA Questions) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 394.89 Td (Q. Why use repositories instead of direct SQL in most places?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 380.89 Td (A. Spring Data JPA repositories reduce boilerplate and provide common CRUD operations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 366.89 Td (with readable method names.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 345.89 Td (Q. Where is a custom database operation used?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 331.89 Td (A. UserRepository has an upsert-style profile sync used by auth-service registration and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 317.89 Td (login recovery.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 296.89 Td (Q. Why validate email uniqueness in UserService?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 282.89 Td (A. It prevents two profiles from sharing the same email and allows the current user to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 268.89 Td (keep their own email during update.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 247.89 Td (Q. What data belongs in auth-service and what belongs in user-service?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 233.89 Td (A. Auth owns credentials, roles, OTP, and JWT. User-service owns profile fields such as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 219.89 Td (name, bio, skills, experience, links, and location.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 46.00 191.89 Td (Feign and Service Communication Questions) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 162.89 Td (Q. Where is Feign used?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 148.89 Td (A. Auth syncs profiles to user-service. Startup, investment, team, and messaging) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 134.89 Td (services fetch user summaries. Investment also calls startup-service.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 113.89 Td (Q. Why not duplicate founder email in Investment entity?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 99.89 Td (A. The source of truth for profile and email data is user-service. Investment stores) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 85.89 Td (business data and fetches profile summary when needed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 64.89 Td (Q. What should happen if Feign call fails during notification?) Tj ET
endstream
