BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 795.89 Td (A. The main operation should usually succeed, and notification failure should be logged) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 781.89 Td (or handled asynchronously.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 46.00 753.89 Td (RabbitMQ Questions) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 724.89 Td (Q. What is NotificationEvent?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 710.89 Td (A. It is a small DTO carrying email and message from producer services to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 696.89 Td (notification-service.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 675.89 Td (Q. Which services publish notifications?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 661.89 Td (A. Auth, startup, investment, team, and messaging services publish notification events.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 640.89 Td (Q. What does @RabbitListener do?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 626.89 Td (A. It subscribes notification-service to the configured queue and invokes the consumer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 612.89 Td (method when events arrive.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 591.89 Td (Q. Why reject without requeue on email failure?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 577.89 Td (A. If credentials or email data are invalid, requeueing forever can create repeated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 563.89 Td (failures and block the queue.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 46.00 535.89 Td (Angular Questions) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 506.89 Td (Q. What is AppStore responsible for?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 492.89 Td (A. It centralizes frontend state, session token, users, startups, investments, invites,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 478.89 Td (messages, notifications, and HTTP methods.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 457.89 Td (Q. How does Angular decide the backend URL?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 443.89 Td (A. resolveApiBase builds http://current-host:8080, so the frontend calls the gateway on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 429.89 Td (the same host.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 408.89 Td (Q. Why store the JWT in frontend state/session?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 394.89 Td (A. The JWT must be added to Authorization headers for protected backend operations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 373.89 Td (Q. What is the advantage of mapping backend DTOs to frontend models?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 359.89 Td (A. The UI can use clean names and types while the backend can keep its own entity and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 345.89 Td (DTO shape.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 46.00 317.89 Td (Testing and Quality Questions) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 288.89 Td (Q. What kinds of tests exist in the project?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 274.89 Td (A. There are controller tests, service tests, repository tests, JWT filter tests, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 260.89 Td (application context tests across services.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 239.89 Td (Q. What is the purpose of SonarQube here?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 225.89 Td (A. SonarQube reports code quality, coverage, duplication, bugs, vulnerabilities, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 211.89 Td (maintainability issues.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 190.89 Td (Q. Why use JaCoCo?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 176.89 Td (A. JaCoCo generates Java test coverage reports that SonarQube can analyze.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 155.89 Td (Q. What would you test in AuthService?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 141.89 Td (A. Registration, duplicate email behavior, OTP expiry, invalid OTP, login before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 127.89 Td (verification, wrong password, role mismatch, JWT generation, and password reset.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 106.89 Td (Q. What would you test in MessagingService?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 92.89 Td (A. Conversation reuse, sender validation, participant validation, message ordering, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 78.89 Td (notification publishing behavior.) Tj ET
endstream
