BT /F2 16 Tf 46.00 785.89 Td (Common Interview Follow-ups) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 756.89 Td (Q. Explain one complete flow from frontend click to database save.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 742.89 Td (A. Example: when a founder creates a startup, the Angular service page calls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 728.89 Td (AppStore.saveStartup\(\). AppStore sends POST /startups to the API Gateway with the JWT) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 714.89 Td (token. The gateway routes the request to startup-service. JwtFilter validates the token) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 700.89 Td (and puts the authenticated user id into SecurityContextHolder. StartupController) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 686.89 Td (receives the request and calls StartupService.create\(\). The service sets id to null,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 672.89 Td (takes founder userId from the authenticated context, saves the Startup entity through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 658.89 Td (StartupRepository into PostgreSQL, optionally publishes a notification event, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 644.89 Td (returns the saved startup to Angular.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 623.89 Td (Q. Show where JWT validation happens and how the authenticated user id is used.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 609.89 Td (A. JWT validation happens in each protected service through its JwtFilter class. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 595.89 Td (filter reads the Authorization header, validates the token using JwtUtil, extracts the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 581.89 Td (subject, and sets Authentication in SecurityContextHolder. Services such as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 567.89 Td (StartupService, InvestmentService, TeamService, and MessagingService read) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 553.89 Td (SecurityContextHolder.getContext\(\).getAuthentication\(\).getName\(\) to get the logged-in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 539.89 Td (user id. This prevents clients from spoofing user ids in request bodies.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 518.89 Td (Q. Explain why notification is asynchronous.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 504.89 Td (A. Notification is asynchronous because email delivery can be slow or fail due to SMTP) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 490.89 Td (or network issues. In FounderLink, business services publish NotificationEvent messages) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 476.89 Td (to RabbitMQ and immediately continue their main operation. notification-service consumes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 462.89 Td (the event later and sends email. This keeps registration, startup creation, investment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 448.89 Td (creation, team invite, and messaging flows fast and resilient.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 427.89 Td (Q. Explain how services communicate with each other.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 413.89 Td (A. The frontend communicates only with API Gateway. The gateway routes HTTP requests to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 399.89 Td (backend services. Backend services communicate synchronously using OpenFeign when they) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 385.89 Td (need immediate data, such as user-service profile summaries or startup-service startup) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 371.89 Td (details. They communicate asynchronously using RabbitMQ for notification events.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 357.89 Td (Services also register with Eureka and read shared configuration from Config Server.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 46.00 336.89 Td (Q. Explain what you would improve if you had more time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 322.89 Td (A. I would improve security, resilience, configuration, and testing. For security, I) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 308.89 Td (would add refresh tokens and stronger method-level role checks. For resilience, I would) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 294.89 Td (add circuit breakers around Feign calls and dead-letter queues for failed RabbitMQ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 280.89 Td (messages. For maintainability, I would add a centralized error response format and use) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 266.89 Td (Docker secrets instead of plain environment passwords. For architecture, I would) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 252.89 Td (consider separate databases per service. For quality, I would add Testcontainers-based) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 58.00 238.89 Td (integration tests for PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ, Redis, and service interactions.) Tj ET
